<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Monastery of Sant Joan de les Abadesses</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 887</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Monastery of Sant Joan de les Abadesses is a religious house in the Ripollès district of Catalonia, founded around 887 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilfred-the-hairy">Wilfred the Hairy</a> for his daughter Emma, its first abbess. One of the earliest nunneries in Catalonia, it anchored the resettlement of the Pyrenean valleys. Its Romanesque church holds a 13th-century wooden Descent from the Cross known as the Santíssim Misteri.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/monastery-of-sant-joan-de-les-abadesses.jpg" alt="Monastery of Sant Joan de les Abadesses" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Xtv · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Claustre_de_Sant_Joan_de_les_Abadesses.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
